      "math_academy_id": "e-2947",
      "problem": "Find the area of the triangle $\\triangle ABC.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14195367/assets/f892cd084f548769fa6b7352fece0e1aef3a66a4ab517ed5b5243d89041ac3a9.png)",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{A} = \\dfrac{b \\cdot h}{2},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $b$ is a base and $h$ is the corresponding height.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the base is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =AB \\\\  & =AH+HB \\\\  & =6+3 \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the corresponding height is\n\n$$\nh={CH} = 4 .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\cdot 4}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{2} \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
